{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"`PostgresIntakeRetryStore.clear_intake_dedup` scoped its delete with `side_effects.c.target.like(f\"%:{repo}\")` at `services/orchestration/intake_retry.py:125`. The repository name is interpolated into a SQL LIKE pattern, where `_` matches any single character and `%` matches any run of characters. GitHub repository names may contain underscores, so a clear for `my_repo` also matches a target belonging to `myXrepo`.\n\nConfirmed against the running database. `select 'ADEV-1:myXrepo' like '%:my_repo'` returns true.\n\nThe consequence is over-deletion on the operator clear path. `inv intake --retry` for one repository removes the `intake_start` ledger row belonging to a different repository that shares the ticket key, which makes that other ticket re-admittable. ADEVX-141 made this ledger row the only guard against a duplicate intake run, so an unintended clear now produces a duplicate run rather than being absorbed by a lingering execution row.\n\n`PostgresIntakeRetryStore` had no unit coverage. The existing tests substitute a `_FakeStore` at the protocol boundary, which bypasses the SQL entirely, so the defect was invisible to the suite.\n\nThe fix applies the repository scope literally rather than as a pattern, reusing the parse helper ADEVX-141 introduced for the same rule in `services/coordination/idempotency.py`. Candidate rows are selected by task id and operation, filtered on the parsed repository suffix in Python, then deleted by exact `side_effect_key`. The no-repository path still clears every `intake_start` row for the ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Clearing intake dedup for a repository whose name contains an underscore leaves another repository's row intact, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_retry.py -k clearing_intake_dedup_treats_underscores_in_the_repo_literally`\n- [ ] Clearing intake dedup without a repository removes every intake row for the ticket, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_retry.py -k clearing_intake_dedup_without_a_repo_clears_every_intake_row`\n- [ ] Clearing intake dedup without a repository leaves other tickets' intake rows intact, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_retry.py -k clearing_intake_dedup_without_a_repo_spares_other_tickets`\n- [ ] Clearing intake dedup for a repository with no matching row deletes nothing, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_retry.py -k clearing_intake_dedup_for_an_unmatched_repo_deletes_nothing`\n- [ ] The repository suffix parser remains shared with the idempotency ledger, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_coordination_idempotency.py -k legacy_intake_repo_match_treats_underscores_literally`\n\n## Testing\nRun each acceptance criterion selector on its own. Run `PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/inv ci` before closing the ticket."}},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1790009998381742001,"uuid":"3f879487-c4bc-4d45-8558-9b6ebb105361"}